 "key_big": "Collect the letters on one side",
 "key_sub": "Clear fractions by multiplying.",
 "body_html": "<h2>How to think about it</h2><ul><li>Move the letter terms to one side and the numbers to the other by doing the same to both sides.</li><li>Expand brackets first.</li><li>To clear fractions, multiply every term by the LCM of the denominators.</li></ul><h2>Examples</h2><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>5x − 3 = 2x + 12</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>3x = 15</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: x = 5</p></div><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>(x + 1)/3 = 4</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>x + 1 = 12</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: x = 11</p></div><h2>Common mistakes</h2><div class='sn-tw'><table class='sn-table'><thead><tr><th>Mistake</th><th>What to do instead</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Changing the sign of only one side</td><td>Do the same to both sides.</td></tr><tr><td>Not multiplying every term</td><td>Multiply each term by the LCM.</td></tr><tr><td>Dividing before collecting terms</td><td>Collect first, then divide.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>",
 "faq": [
